    "result_text": "There's only one test class in the repo, and it passes. The build is green.\n\n## Summary\n\nImplemented `capacityWarning` on owner responses, returning `true` when the owner's city already holds **40\u201349** owners (approaching the 50 hard limit), following the existing `bulkSignupWarning` pattern.\n\nChanges:\n\n1. **`src/main/resources/openapi.yml`** \u2014 added a read-only `capacityWarning` boolean to the `Owner` schema (generates `OwnerDto.setCapacityWarning(...)`), documented as true for cities holding 40\u201349 owners.\n\n2. **`OwnerRestControllerV1.java`**:\n   - Extracted the case-insensitive per-city count into a shared `countOwnersInCity(String)` helper (now used by both the hard rejection and the warning, so they measure occupancy identically).\n   - Added `CITY_CAPACITY_WARNING_THRESHOLD = 40L` and a `capacityWarning(String city)` helper returning true when `count >= 40 && count < 50` (null city never warns).\n   - Stamped `capacityWarning` in `toOwnerDtoWithWarning(...)`, so it appears on the create (201), read (200), and idempotent-replay responses alongside `bulkSignupWarning`.\n\nThe hard rejection at 50 (`CITY_OWNER_CAPACITY`, `rejectCityAtCapacity`) is unchanged. `AcceptanceTest.coreWarnsWhenApproachingCapacity` and `mvn test` both pass (`BUILD SUCCESS`).",
